# Triple-filtered hashish — loose blonde powder, the cleanest thing the screen makes.
#
# PLACEHOLDER art. Warlon Mhite may redraw it; that is what this file is for.
#
# ## Three items, three forms, and the silhouette is what tells them apart
#
#   item/hashish   an oblique slab   pressed in a mould    brown
#   item/charas    an irregular ball hand-rolled           near-black
#   item/filtered  a loose heap      never pressed at all  blonde
#
# So this one is a low mound with a broken, granular top edge — the shape of a pile of powder
# tipped out, not a solid object. That matters more than the palette does: the family must never
# read as one item in three shades, because the three are not a ladder. Colour follows process,
# and nothing in this mod claims a colour means a number.
#
# Blonde because less oxidation and less leaf through the screen really is blonder. It is sampled
# up from the kief tones in dry_sifter.mctex rather than invented, so the powder in the block and
# the powder in your hand are the same material — but at item contrast, not block contrast.

@palette default
. = none
1 = 4A3418      the shadow under the heap, and its rim
2 = 6B4E24
3 = 8A6A33
4 = A98844      the body of the heap
5 = C9A566      the strain entry's own colour — the lit face
6 = E0C089      grains catching the light
7 = F2DBAE      the brightest grains; scattered, never a band

@texture item/filtered_hashish 16x16 type=item
